  "reason": "The current best (config_025: scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, transformer, weighted, acc=0.725) establishes that multiprofile + scvi_n200 + transformer aggregation + weighted fusion is the strongest combination. However, the image encoder dimension remains unexplored in this top-performing setup—every high-accuracy experiment used imagenet_vit_l. config_034 isolates the image encoder variable by swapping imagenet_vit_l → resnet50 while holding all other settings at their best-known values. This is the highest-uncertainty, highest-impact question remaining: if resnet50 matches or beats ViT-L, it opens a new axis of improvement; if it lags significantly, it confirms ViT-L is optimal and lets us redirect remaining budget to the RNA encoder (pca_n2000) or fine-tuning aggregation. With 4 experiments left after this, resolving the image encoder question is the best use of the next slot to guide final exploitation."
}

